# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]   (no dollar/backtick in the text)
register_gate "tests/test_schema_false_couple.py" "SCHEMA FALSE-COUPLE GATE: PASS" "schema false-couple precision" "the ORM/DDL extractors do not mint FALSE tables (a false table becomes a false cross-substrate coupling and now a false PAUSE): the @Entity bridge is line-anchored so an inline comment on the decorator line cannot leak comment words as tables, the Sequelize .init tableName pattern requires sequelize to co-occur so a non-Sequelize .init({tableName}) mints nothing, SQL comments are stripped before the DDL scan so commented-out/rollback DDL mints no ghost table, a Rails column-DDL method (add_column/add_index) INSIDE a create_table/change_table/.table block does NOT mint the COLUMN name as a table, and prose-FROM mints no edge because no false table exists to hit; each real pattern still extracts (recall preserved)" "schema false-couple precision (precision audit residue): five extractor over-coupling sources that now cause false PAUSEs are closed. A: _ORM_JPA_ENTITY_RE was re.S with a newline-crossing gap that matched class name / class definition inside an inline comment on the @Entity line, minting English words as tables -> now line-anchored to the decorator line then the real class. B: the Sequelize tableName .init pattern fired on any .init({tableName}) (connect-pg-simple, express-mysql-session, bookshelf) -> now requires sequelize in the same options. C: the .sql DDL scan did not strip comments, so commented-out rollback DDL (-- CREATE TABLE old_x, block comments) minted ghost tables -> SQL comments are stripped first. D: a Rails column-DDL method INSIDE a create_table/change_table/.table do block (discourse Schema.table :uploads do, add_column :url, :text) minted the COLUMN names (url/type/path/data/message) as false low-participant tables that slip past hub dampening -> the Rails column-DDL methods are now block-aware (the first symbol is a table ONLY at top level; inside a table-DSL block it is a column and the enclosing opener mints the real table). Measured on discourse: 28 false generic tables removed, real tables gain touchers, genuine couples preserved. A top-level add_column inside def up / class is unchanged (recall). E: the prose-FROM false edge (Creating posts from message batches -> queries message) only fired because a FALSE message table existed; with D fixed the prose word has no known table to hit and the known-table guard drops it WITHOUT tightening the FROM regex (a name-based FROM tightening was MEASURED recall-unsafe on real repos: it drops multi-line heredoc SQL, UPDATE-FROM, and short-aliased FROM t a couples). E pins both directions: prose mints no edge; a real SELECT FROM orders still does. Offline, no Postgres; each finding asserts the false table is gone AND the real pattern still extracts (recall kept). Existing EXTRACTOR / SCHEMA PRECISION / JS-ORM / ORM-DSL / COLUMN-SUBSTRATE / ECTO gates stay green." 16
